{
  "inShort": "The checkpoint ended behind: the playable-slice goal was missed. Sprint 4 shared no playable build or five-player notes, so two islands, tides and co-op remain unverified. Mia has not confirmed work since week one, leaving Alex alone confirming work toward the slice.",
  "discussed": [
    {
      "itemId": "cmvu35sa101am4gz8x0m11qfx",
      "text": "A public repository of the Godot demo projects the game builds on is done. The checked repository contains demo folders, an MIT license and import instructions. It supplies reference projects, not evidence of the playable slice."
    },
    {
      "itemId": "cmvu35sd201an4gz82vgs6mq3",
      "text": "An animated reference video for the art style remains done. The title and thumbnail identify Big Buck Bunny. The video was not watched, so its animation and suitability remain unchecked."
    },
    {
      "itemId": "cmvu35sg701aq4gz890icklg1",
      "text": "A reference article on what playtesting is, for the team to read is done. The checked Wikipedia article explains playtesting and its formats. It does not show that five players tested this game."
    },
    {
      "itemId": "cmvu35shi01ar4gz8cnvwlh43",
      "text": "A private design board for the team remains done. Its contents were not checked, so it cannot establish a chosen style."
    }
  ],
  "notDiscussed": [],
  "outsidePlan": [
    "The published prototype devlog satisfies the stage’s sole requirement. The stage is passed, despite the missed checkpoint goal.",
    "The devlog reports polish, an uploaded build and a finished video. No build artifact was added. The image shows mountains, and the linked video is identified as Big Buck Bunny. Neither demonstrates the islands, tide loop or co-op sailing."
  ],
  "questions": [
    "What can you verify about the playable slice without a shared build?",
    "What did each of the five players complete, where did they struggle, and who tested co-op?"
  ]
}

